# Committed on purpose — no real secrets. Mirrors the repo root's own
# ".env.test" (see ../../.env.test), but scoped here specifically to make
# sure it wins over this same directory's own ".env": NestJS's
# ConfigModule.forRoot({ envFilePath }) in app.module.ts checks
# ".env.<NODE_ENV>" *before* plain ".env", so with NODE_ENV=test this file
# always overrides apps/api/.env's CRM_DRIVER — even though that file
# deliberately sets CRM_DRIVER=postgres for real local development (so the
# dev server shows the real corporate catalog).
#
# Ordinary test runs (npm test, npm run test:e2e) must never reach the
# real, external CRM database — only MockCrmClientRepository. A dedicated,
# separately-run CRM integration check (npm run test:crm-integration) opts
# back into CRM_DRIVER=postgres explicitly via ALLOW_REAL_CRM_IN_TESTS=true.
CRM_DRIVER=mock
